# Tests

## Running Tests

From outside the devcontainer:
```bash
docker exec -u vscode -w /workspaces/<%= app_name %> <%= container_name %> bash -ic "bin/rails test"
docker exec -u vscode -w /workspaces/<%= app_name %> <%= container_name %> bash -ic "bin/rails test test/models/user_test.rb"
docker exec -u vscode -w /workspaces/<%= app_name %> <%= container_name %> bash -ic "bin/rails test test/models/user_test.rb:42"
```

Inside the devcontainer:
```bash
bin/rails test
bin/rails test test/models/user_test.rb
bin/rails test test/models/user_test.rb:42
```

## Conventions

### General
- Minitest + Capybara (not RSpec)
- Write tests before implementation (TDD enforced by hooks)
- One assertion per test method when practical
- Descriptive test names: `test "user with no email is invalid"`

### Model Tests
```ruby
class UserTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
  test "validates presence of email" do
    user = build(:user, email: nil)
    assert_not user.valid?
    assert_includes user.errors[:email], "can't be blank"
  end
end
```

### Controller Tests
```ruby
class UsersControllerTest < ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest
  test "index returns success" do
    get users_url
    assert_response :success
  end
end
```

### System Tests
```ruby
class SignUpFlowTest < ApplicationSystemTestCase
  test "user can sign up" do
    visit new_user_registration_path
    fill_in "Email", with: "test@example.com"
    fill_in "Password", with: "password123"
    fill_in "Password confirmation", with: "password123"
    click_on "Sign up"
    assert_text "Welcome"
  end
end
```

### Service Tests
```ruby
class MyServiceTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
  test "performs successfully" do
    result = MyService.call(param: "value")
    assert result.success?
  end
end
```

### What to Avoid
- Don't test framework behavior (Rails validations themselves work; test your validation rules)
- Don't test private methods directly
- Don't use `sleep` in tests; use Capybara's built-in waiting
- Don't create test data manually when a factory exists

